Let $y_0(\theta), y_1(\theta), y_2(\theta), \ldots$ be the sequence of ratings received by the seller of type $\theta$.  The {\em aggregate score} up to time $k$ of this seller is the average score from ratings received:
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:aggscore}
 x_k(\theta) =  \frac{1}{n_k(\theta)} \sum_{\ell = 0}^{n_k(\theta)} \phi(y_\ell(\theta)).
\end{equation}
(We presume $x_0(\theta) = 0$ for all $\theta$.)  Since $\phi(y) \in [0,1]$ for all $y$, the score $x_k$ also lies in $[0,1]$.

